           <div type="translation">
            <p></p></div>

            <div type="commentary">
            <p>F. G. Bewer: "The stamp is cast in one piece, probably by the indirect lost-wax
                    process from a stamped mold. The lettering is very fine, although some letters
                    flow into each other. The uneven surface may be due to a casting flaw, wear, or
                    corrosion; it is in otherwise good condition. The patina is reddish brown with
                    fine green-black speckles, some cuprite, and gray and tan burial
                    accretions."</p></div>
            

